# report-builder-AI-ipynb

A production-oriented framework to convert notebook outputs into professional company reports using AI-assisted summarization with **output-first reporting**.

## What it does

- Uses original notebook results (text, tables, charts/visual descriptions) as primary report content
- Adds concise AI-generated executive summary (Claude/GPT/any model via pluggable adapter)
- Generates **both PDF and DOCX** outputs
- Supports audience modes:
  - `business`
  - `technical`
  - `business_technical`
- Supports company branding (logo + company name)
- Designed to be platform-agnostic (works with Databricks exports and any JSON payload that maps outputs)

## Install

```bash
pip install -e .
```

## Input schema (example)

```json
{
  "outputs": [
    {"type": "text", "title": "Observation", "content": "Model A outperformed baseline by 14%."},
    {"type": "table", "title": "Metrics", "content": "Metric|Value\nAccuracy|0.92\nRecall|0.89"},
    {"type": "chart", "title": "Trend", "content": "Weekly trend shows stable growth."}
  ]
}
```

## Usage

```bash
report-builder \
  --input notebook_outputs.json \
  --title "Q3 Notebook Insights" \
  --company "Example Corp" \
  --audience business_technical \
  --logo ./assets/logo.png \
  --output-dir ./reports
```

Outputs:
- `reports/q3-notebook-insights.pdf`
- `reports/q3-notebook-insights.docx`

## AI integration

Use `report_builder.ai.AIAdapter` to plug in Claude/GPT provider clients while keeping data flow and renderers unchanged.
